      <details style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin-bottom:12px;">
        <summary style="color:white;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-size:1.05rem;">Which is cheaper: BirkyStudio or Dialpad?</summary>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-top:12px;">
          For a solo agent, BirkyStudio is cheaper. At $550 setup + ~$30-50/mo, your first year costs ~$910-$1,150. Dialpad's Standard plan is $23/user/mo ($276/year) but doesn't include AI receptionist features — you'd need their Support plan at $75+/user/mo ($900+/year). For teams of 5+, Dialpad's per-user pricing becomes more competitive, but BirkyStudio doesn't scale to multi-user phone systems.
